  "body": "According to https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-control-infrastructure.html#implicit-submission:\r\n>A form element's default button is the first submit button in tree order whose form owner is that form element.\r\n\r\nToday I discovered that this behaviour changes between browsers depending on whether the first submit button is displayed or not. For example, if the first submit button is set to `display: none;` then Safari will skip it and choose the next submit button, whereas Chrome will choose the first one.\r\n\r\nAfter some thought I believe the CSS display property should not effect the DOM (and hence the undisplayed button should still be found first in tree order) and therefore this is a bug in Safari. As such I have submitted a bug report to Apple about it.\r\n\r\nThat being said, it took me a while to reach that conclusion. Can this section be made a little clearer about correct behaviour or would doing so just add unnecessary verbiage?",
